body:
Following up on https://github.com/apache/iceberg/issues/2554.
We should enable dropping HMS tables even if the metadata files have been corrupted/deleted in the meantime.
@RussellSpitzer @rdblue @pvary

This should allow the 5.2.x releases to support temporal filter requests.

@CarstenHollmann I noticed that the temporal duration filter support was on `develop` and the 6.x branch, but not on the stable 5.2.x branch.

So I cherry-picked the changes from `develop` into `maintenance/5.2.x`.

Hi,
After discussion with Slavi ([link to private chat](https://matrix.to/#/!GWNJzoHiCybWdouIiP:etke.cc/$_XpK8-ucbWvxY667IVZ9ROZPqSVkG2UGglNagrbDQmw?via=etke.cc&via=devture.com)), we agreed on adding services that use matrix-docker-ansible-deploy as a core to list in README file.

@GoMatrixHosting could you approve the description is correct, please? (Sorry, I just put what I know about your service)

1.  Added new command: `nctl-exec-upgrade-scenario-1`;
2.  Scenario attempts to: spin-up a network; roll-out an upgrade; join passive nodes.
3.  Scenario performs assertions at each step.
